PASS A1 z3: sigma>=|p| => DEC for every observer |v|<1 (negation unsat)
PASS A2 z3: sigma>=0, sigma<|p| => explicit violating observer exists (negation unsat)
PASS A3 z3: sigma<0 => rest observer violates (unsat)
PASS A4 z3: for p>0, [sigma>=0 & sigma>=|p|] <=> sigma-p>=0 (negation unsat)
PASS A5 z3: for p<0, sigma-p>=0 does NOT imply DEC (sat=sat, e.g. [sigma = 0, p = -1/2])
PASS A6 z3: the 4D normal eigenvalue 0 adds nothing (sigma>=|p| => sigma>=|0|) (unsat)
PASS B1 sympy: stationary point of gamma(sigma - v p) at v = p/sigma: [p/sigma]
PASS B2 sympy: its minimum is sqrt(sigma^2-p^2) (got sqrt(-p**2 + sigma**2))
PASS B3 sympy: per-gamma margin (sigma - v p) -> sigma - p as v->1 (got -p + sigma)
PASS B4: sqrt(s^2-p^2)=sqrt((s-p)(s+p)) so sign(sigma-p) = DEC sign for sigma,p>0 (magnitude is convention)
PASS C1 sympy: sigma_0 = (1-s)/(4 pi R) (got (1 - s)/(4*pi*R))
PASS C2 sympy: p_0 = (1-s)^2/(16 pi R s) (got (s - 1)**2/(16*pi*R*s))
PASS C3: p_0 > 0 for every s in (0,1), i.e. every x in (0,1): the 'p>0' hypothesis holds at the static point
PASS C4 sympy: 8 pi R (sigma_0 - p_0) == Le Eq (17) -(5s-1)(s-1)/(2s)
PASS C5: margin zeros at s in [1/5, 1] -> interior zero s=1/5, x = 1 - 1/25 = 24/25
PASS C6: margin > 0 on s in (1/5,1) (x<24/25), < 0 on (0,1/5)
PASS D1 sympy: closed-form sigma(R) solves sigma' = -2(sigma+p)/R
PASS D2 sympy: sigma(R0) = sigma0
PASS D3 sympy: sigma + p = (sigma0+p0) r^(-2(1+beta2))  > 0 at every finite R, -> 0
PASS D4 sympy: sigma - p = (1-beta2)(sigma0+p0)/(1+beta2) r^(-2A) + 2 sigma_inf
PASS D5 sympy: d(sigma-p)/dR = (1-beta2) sigma'  (tree wall.py:205-206)
PASS D6 sympy: lim_{R->inf}(sigma-p) = 2(beta2 sigma0 - p0)/(1+beta2) (tree wall.py:377-381)
PASS D7 sympy: lim p = -sigma_inf (got (-beta2*sigma0 + p0)/(beta2 + 1)): when the basin is 'unbounded' (sigma_inf>0), p ends NEGATIVE
